> Anyway, I found myself a chest and dropped a slew of
> potions, scrolls, possibly cursed armor, etc in there.  (Not the best
> choice, but I was trying to unburden myself.)  I knew it's a wise idea
> to engrave the E-word on the square the chest is in to help protect it.

If you do not intend to visit the level again and wander around, you
can drag the box next to the down staircase, and make your stash there.

While your character is away from a level, that level's monsters do not
move. Things that will rot/deteriorate will still rot/deteriorate
though.

But if you ever come back to the level and want to leave the box out of
your sight, you will need to pick the box or all contents up.

IIRC no monsters can open chests... so the only danger is something ate
it (e.g. gelatinous cube), or something strong enough to pick the chest
up (e.g. your pet when your chest is not very heavy yet).

For a safer stash then yes, you'll want to engrave Elbereth underneath.
But know that monsters are not the only thing that will destroy your
stash, especially if you're not careful. ;)

